You are a web developer. Fix the bug in the following code.

BUG DESCRIPTION: A component registers a window resize listener repeatedly and never cleans it up, causing a listener leak across rerenders and unmounts.

CODE:
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';

export default function ResizeTracker() {
  const [width, setWidth] = useState(window.innerWidth);
  const [ticks, setTicks] = useState(0);

  useEffect(() => {
    const handleResize = () => {
      setWidth(window.innerWidth);
    };

    window.addEventListener('resize', handleResize);
  });

  return (
    <div>
      <div data-testid="width">{width}</div>
      <button type="button" onClick={() => setTicks((current) => current + 1)}>
        Rerender {ticks}
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}

CONSTRAINTS:
- Fix the bug while preserving existing functionality
- Do not rewrite the entire component
- Return the complete fixed file

IMPORTANT:
- Return ONLY the code. No explanations.
- Output a single complete file.
